  "text": "Their diagnostic modeling task arrived Sunday afternoon. A neighborhood food cooperative wanted to offer produce boxes at several prices. Students had to create a model showing how the number of subscribers could affect weekly revenue. The prompt included a tiny data table and just enough ambiguity to start an argument. Malik built formulas immediately. Nia turned the page sideways and drew three families standing near a bus stop. We have forty minutes, he said. I know. Then why are there people? Because people buy the boxes.",
